**CONTROL FLOW – INTRO & IF**

// =============================
//* 1️⃣ What is Control Flow?
// =============================
// Control Flow decides which part of code will run.
// It helps programs make decisions based on conditions.

Example:
if (condition) {
  // code runs only if condition is true
}

// =============================
//* 2️⃣ IF Statement
// =============================
int age = 18;

if (age >= 18) {
  print("You are eligible to vote.");
}

int age = 20;

if (age >= 18) {
  print("You are eligible to vote.");
}

Explanation:
👉 The if statement checks the condition (age >= 18) — if true, it runs the code inside {}.

Example 2: if with a false condition

int marks = 30;

if (marks > 40) {
  print("You passed!");
}

print("Exam finished!");

Output:
Exam finished!
Because marks > 40 is false, the code inside if doesn’t run.

// Output: You are eligible to vote.

**IF-ELSE STATEMENT**

Definition:
When you want to do one thing if a condition is true, and something else if false.

if (condition) {
  // runs if true
} else {
  // runs if false
}

int age = 16;

if (age >= 18) {
  print("You can vote.");
} else {
  print("You are too young to vote.");
}


int marks = 80;

if (marks >= 50) {
  print("Passed");
} else {
  print("Failed");
}


Example:
int marks = 40;
if (marks >= 35) {
  print("Pass");
} else {
  print("Fail");
}


**IF-ELSE-IF LADDER**

Used when multiple conditions exist.

Used when you have multiple conditions to check — one by one.

Example:
int marks = 85;
if (marks >= 90) {
  print("Grade A+");
} else if (marks >= 75) {
  print("Grade A");
} else if (marks >= 60) {
  print("Grade B");
} else {
  print("Fail");
}

int temperature = 25;

if (temperature > 35) {
  print("It's hot!");
} else if (temperature > 20) {
  print("It's pleasant!");
} else {
  print("It's cold!");
}

